# Line endings are content here, not a style preference.
#
# Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its SYSTEM config, so without
# this file a fresh clone on Windows checks text out with CRLF. A reference
# document's bytes are its store cost and a program's hash, and a map's
# documents are raw strings, so a checkout must hand every tool LF.
# Mirrors the engine's `.gitattributes`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Art and sound are bytes, never text.
*.png  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.dmi  binary
*.wasm binary
*.ico  binary
*.ase  binary
*.aseprite binary
*.woff2 binary
